    {
      "id": "spin-box-compute-exponent-slider-fraction",
      "name": "SpinBoxComputeExponentSliderFraction",
      "category": "SSpinBox",
      "signature": "SpinBoxComputeExponentSliderFraction(Target, Fraction Filled, Start Fraction Filled, Slider Exponent)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SSpinBox*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Fraction Filled",
          "type": "Float"
        },
        {
          "name": "Start Fraction Filled",
          "type": "Float"
        },
        {
          "name": "Slider Exponent",
          "type": "Float"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Float",
      "docs": "This function compute a slider position by simulating two log on both side of the neutral value\nExample a slider going from 0.0 to 2.0 with a neutral value of 1.0, the user will have a lot of precision around the neutral value\non both side.\n|\n||                              |\n| -_                          _-\n|   --__                  __--\n|       ----__________----\n----------------------------------\n0              1               2\nThe function return a float representing the slider fraction used to position the slider handle\nFractionFilled: this is the value slider position with no exponent\nStartFractionFilled: this is the neutral value slider position with no exponent\nSliderExponent: this is the slider exponent"
    },
